/* Copyright 2026 Rhett Creighton - Apache License 2.0
 *
 * blocker_operator_decisions — the OTHER half of a named blocker.
 *
 * Why this exists
 * ----------------
 * blocker_remedy_bindings.def already answers "does anything in the tree
 * attempt a cure for this id?" — a condition healer, an ESCAPE(action), or
 * the honest token OWNER. That table is a build-time ratchet and it works.
 * What it cannot answer is the question the operator actually has when a
 * blocker is bound OWNER: *what am I supposed to decide?*
 *
 * A reason that is honest and specific but offers the reader nothing to do
 * teaches an operator to ignore alarms, which destroys the property this
 * codebase is built around (a stall is always a named blocker, never a
 * silent stop).
 *
 * So: every row here states, in plain words, the decision a person owns and
 * the tradeoff between the options. It is deliberately NOT a place to
 * invent an automatic repair. Several of these blockers genuinely require
 * judgment — spending hours of bandwidth, or installing a state artifact
 * this node has not independently verified — and a wrong automatic remedy
 * on consensus-adjacent state is far worse than an honest hand-off.
 *
 * Row format
 * ----------
 *   ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(id_or_pattern, "text")
 *
 * `id_or_pattern` uses the SAME glob rule as blocker_remedy_bindings.def
 * (`*` = any run of characters), matched by the one shared implementation,
 * codeindex_emit_glob_match(). An exact id beats a pattern; among patterns
 * the longest match wins, so `coin_backfill.unprovable.*` outranks
 * `coin_backfill.*`.
 *
 * `text` is a static string literal rendered verbatim into
 * `dumpstate blocker` as `operator_decision`. It should name the options
 * and their costs; it must not restate the reason (the blocker already
 * carries that, with the live heights filled in).
 *
 * This table is ADDITIVE and intentionally NOT a totality ratchet: a row is
 * written when someone has actually read the raise site and can state the
 * decision truthfully. An OWNER-bound blocker with no row here renders
 * `needs_human: true` with an empty `operator_decision` and is counted in
 * `undeclared_decision_count` — visible debt, never a silent gap. Inventing
 * plausible-sounding decision text for a raise site nobody read would be
 * worse than the empty string, because it would look answered.
 *
 * Rows are only meaningful for ids bound OWNER in blocker_remedy_bindings.
 * def; an id with a real auto-remedy renders `remedy_kind: automatic` and
 * needs no decision. */

#ifndef ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION
#error "define ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(id_or_pattern, text) before including blocker_operator_decisions.def"
#endif

/* ── Optional shielded proving capability (engine/composition/src/boot_params_gate.c).
 * Consensus validation remains armed from embedded verifying keys; only
 * transaction creation requiring the large proving parameters is absent. */
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(utxo_apply.value_overflow_owner_gate,
    "utxo_apply holds at a value_overflow hole because the only repair "
    "rewinds the coin frontier to re-apply that block, and that rewind "
    "mutates consensus state. "
    "OPTION A - copy the datadir, set ZCL_REDUCER_VALUE_OVERFLOW_REPAIR_ACK=1 "
    "for the node running on the COPY, restart it, and let the repair run "
    "there; it refuses a genuinely invalid block and never rewinds past a "
    "moved cursor. Promote the copy only after it passes the same tip and "
    "commitment checks. Cost: disk for the copy and a supervised restart. "
    "OPTION B - leave the node held. Nothing is rewritten, but utxo_apply "
    "does not advance past the hole, so everything downstream of it stays "
    "behind until A is done or the datadir is rebuilt from a verified "
    "snapshot. There is deliberately no automatic path: the ack exists so "
    "that no consensus rewind runs without a person choosing it.")
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(shielded_spend_unavailable,
    "A person must choose whether this node needs to create shielded "
    "transactions. OPTION A - install the four pinned proving-parameter files "
    "using tools/scripts/zcash_params.sh as documented in docs/PARAMS.md. "
    "Cost: several GiB of trusted local storage and an explicit verified "
    "installation. OPTION B - leave them absent. The node continues validating "
    "and serving shielded consensus data, but refuses every operation that "
    "would require creating a shielded proof. Consensus sync and transparent "
    "transactions are unaffected.")

/* A validation stage held because a check keeps running out of memory on this
 * host (engine/jobs/src/stage_db_fault.c); permanent after the memory budget. */
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(*.local_out_of_memory,
    "A person must give this node enough memory or move it. OPTION A - stop "
    "other memory-heavy work on the host or raise the node's memory limit; the "
    "held stage retries and clears itself on its next pass that does not run "
    "out of memory. Cost: host capacity taken from other work. OPTION B - move "
    "the node to a host with more memory. Cost: a node move and its downtime. "
    "While held the node writes no verdict, marks no block invalid, scores no "
    "peer and never escalates to a reindex, so waiting is safe, but the held "
    "stage stays stopped at the held height (for bg_validation only background "
    "re-verification stops; sync continues).")

/* ── Projection index coverage floor (engine/services/src/index_fold_guard.c,
 * raised for address_index / txindex / op_return_index). ─────────────── */
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(*.below_snapshot_seed,
    "A person must choose; the node will not choose for you. This datadir was "
    "seeded from a UTXO snapshot, so block bodies BELOW the seed height were "
    "never downloaded. This index folds forward only and has no source to read "
    "across that floor, and no safe automatic repair exists: synthesizing index "
    "rows for blocks the node cannot read would be fabricating data. "
    "OPTION A - backfill the historical bodies below the seed floor from peers. "
    "The blocker then clears on its own and the index covers the whole chain. "
    "Cost: a full historical body download, several GB of disk and hours of "
    "bandwidth competing with tip sync. "
    "OPTION B - accept partial coverage. The index serves heights at or above "
    "the seed floor and answers nothing below it; pass -<index>=0 to stop the "
    "fold and retire this blocker entirely. Cost: pre-seed history is "
    "unqueryable through this index. "
    "Consensus is unaffected either way - address_index, txindex and "
    "op_return_index are rebuildable projections, never consensus state, and "
    "this blocker never holds the reducer frontier.")

/* ── Declared partial coverage (engine/services/src/index_fold_guard.c,
 * index_fold_declare_partial_coverage). The successor to the spin above for
 * op_return_index: the projection ADOPTS the seed floor as its declared base
 * and folds forward from it, so it makes progress and its digest states the
 * range it covers. Raised once per adoption, not per tick. ───────────── */
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(*.partial_coverage,
    "Nothing is stuck; this is a standing coverage declaration a person owns. "
    "The index adopted the snapshot-seed floor as its base and is folding "
    "forward from it, and its running digest carries base_height/base_digest so "
    "no verifier can mistake this range commitment for a whole-chain one. "
    "OPTION A - accept it (the default, and what the node is doing now). The "
    "index answers every height at or above the base and answers nothing below "
    "it. Cost: pre-seed history is unqueryable through this index, and any "
    "anchor published from this digest commits to the declared range only. "
    "OPTION B - buy the history: backfill the pre-seed block bodies from peers, "
    "then rebuild the index from genesis (`z23 app oprindex rebuild`). "
    "The base returns to 0 and this declaration retires. Cost: a full "
    "historical body download, several GB of disk and hours of bandwidth "
    "competing with tip sync. "
    "Consensus is unaffected either way - these are rebuildable projections, "
    "never consensus state, and this blocker never holds the reducer frontier.")

/* ── Torn body position (engine/services/src/index_fold_guard.c,
 * index_fold_note_unreadable_body). NOT the same wall as below_snapshot_seed:
 * there the body was never downloaded; here the index SAYS it has the body and
 * the bytes at that position are something else. Typical cause: blk*.dat
 * hardlinked into a running foreign node's datadir, whose appends overwrite
 * records this node already indexed. ────────────────────────────────── */
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(*.body_unreadable,
    "A person must choose; the node will not choose for you. The block index "
    "flags this height BLOCK_HAVE_DATA and names a position in a blk*.dat file, "
    "but the bytes there are not that block. Retrying cannot fix it - the "
    "backfill was re-reading the same dead position every tick until this "
    "blocker replaced the spin - and no safe automatic repair exists at a "
    "height this far below the fold frontier. "
    "FIRST, check whether the blk*.dat files are shared: `stat` them and look "
    "at the link count. A blk file hardlinked into another running node's "
    "datadir is rewritten under this node, which is exactly how a hash-valid "
    "position goes dead. If so, stop sharing the files before repairing "
    "anything, or the repair will be undone. "
    "OPTION A - re-point the index at a surviving copy. If the block still "
    "exists elsewhere in the blk files, the hash-targeted rescan "
    "(block_index_repair_pos_from_disk) finds it and re-stores the position "
    "through the verified path. Cost: a scan of the blk set. "
    "OPTION B - clear BLOCK_HAVE_DATA for the height and let the body be "
    "re-fetched from peers. Cost: bandwidth, and it only works while some peer "
    "still serves that height. "
    "OPTION C - accept partial coverage below the affected range (-<index>=0). "
    "Cost: that history is unqueryable through this index. "
    "Consensus is unaffected - these are rebuildable projections, never "
    "consensus state, and this blocker never holds the reducer frontier.")

/* ── Full-history authority publication
 * (engine/services/src/bg_validation_authority.c). The live blocker reason names
 * the exact missing proof or moving frontier; no trust override exists. ─── */
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(bg_validation.full_history_unproven,
    "A person must choose; the node will not convert an incomplete historical "
    "walk into durable trust. Read the live reason first. "
    "OPTION A - preserve the datadir, restore or fetch every missing block body "
    "and undo record (or restore the required root-bound snapshot evidence), "
    "then rerun the validation campaign against a synchronized frontier. Cost: "
    "history download, disk, and proof/script verification time. The blocker "
    "clears only after exact tip and coins commitments agree with zero coverage "
    "or script skips. "
    "OPTION B - keep this datadir in assisted/bootstrap-trust posture. It may "
    "continue serving under local policy, but it cannot provide FULLY_VALIDATED "
    "evidence or qualify a release. "
    "There is deliberately no accept-anyway option: doing so would turn a "
    "missing consensus proof into an owner assertion.")

/* ── Recovery-ladder escape hatches (engine/services/src/sticky_escalator.c).
 * Raised when the self-heal routes ran and failed because the artifact they
 * wanted does not exist. ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(sticky_escalator.resnapshot_no_base,
    "A person must choose. The rewind-to-a-self-verified-base rung ran and "
    "found nothing to rewind to: this node has minted no self-valid seal yet, "
    "and the compiled SHA3 checkpoint is a proven HASH rather than loadable "
    "STATE, so it only serves as a base when its snapshot artifact is present "
    "on disk - it is not. Nothing running in the node produces that artifact; "
    "it comes from the anchor mint/export path or a fetched checkpoint bundle. "
    "OPTION A - supply the verified utxo-anchor.snapshot for the compiled "
    "checkpoint height, after which this rung has a base and rewinds on the "
    "next escalation. Cost: obtaining and validating an external artifact. "
    "OPTION B - do nothing. The escalator already falls through to the durable "
    "from-bodies rungs (reindex / self_mint_refold), which re-derive forward "
    "over on-disk bodies and need no artifact. Cost: substantially slower. "
    "Never auto-attempted: manufacturing a base would mean adopting state this "
    "node has not verified, which is the one thing the cure path forbids.")

ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(sticky_escalator.refold_no_anchor_artifact,
    "A person must choose. The refold-from-anchor rung refused to arm because "
    "the verified anchor snapshot - utxo-anchor.snapshot, bound to the compiled "
    "SHA3 checkpoint - is not reachable from this datadir. Arming without it "
    "would make the next boot FATAL-refuse at the reset, so refusing to arm is "
    "the correct behaviour, not a fault. That artifact is produced by the "
    "anchor mint/export path or fetched as a checkpoint bundle; no running "
    "subsystem creates it. "
    "OPTION A - place the SHA3-checkpoint-bound utxo-anchor.snapshot in the "
    "datadir; the rung then arms itself on the next escalation cycle. "
    "OPTION B - leave it absent and let the reindex rung re-derive from genesis "
    "over on-disk bodies. Cost: a full re-fold instead of an anchor jump. "
    "Never auto-fetched: a borrowed state artifact is installable only after "
    "independent validation of its transparent and shielded contents - matching "
    "a header height or hash is not enough.")

ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(sticky_escalator.resnapshot_no_consumer,
    "A person must decide, but this is a BUILD fact, not an operator toggle. A "
    "self-verified rewind base IS reachable, yet no in-process rewind consumer "
    "(stage_rederive_range, or the seal window_rebuild) is linked into this "
    "binary, so the rung cannot use the base it found. "
    "OPTION A - run a binary built with the rewind consumer linked. "
    "OPTION B - accept the fall-through to the durable reindex/refold rungs, "
    "which is what the escalator already does. "
    "Nothing to auto-attempt: a symbol that is not linked cannot be supplied at "
    "runtime.")

ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(body_persist.body_unfetchable,
    "A person must choose. body_persist needs the block body at a height AT OR "
    "BELOW the active chain tip, and those bytes are not on disk. It cannot "
    "ask the network for them: the header-driven body queue only ever requests "
    "heights strictly ABOVE the tip, so this height is unreachable by re-fetch "
    "and the stage will hold here indefinitely rather than advance past a body "
    "it never validated. The usual cause is a truncated or removed blk*.dat, "
    "or a datadir copied without its block files - genesis itself is seeded at "
    "boot on every network and is no longer a source of this hold. "
    "OPTION A - run with -reindex. The on-disk block files are rescanned and "
    "the index re-derived from what is genuinely present, which lowers the tip "
    "to the last body actually held so every missing height above it becomes "
    "requestable again. Cost: a full rescan of the block files. "
    "OPTION B - replace the datadir's block files from a source that has them, "
    "then restart. Cost: obtaining and trusting an external copy; the bodies "
    "are re-validated against their headers on the way in either way. "
    "Never auto-attempted: the only automatic escape would be rewinding the "
    "active tip so the height becomes requestable, and silently moving the tip "
    "to work around missing data is a chain-state mutation the node must not "
    "make on its own.")

/* ── Deep-reorg refusal (engine/jobs/src/utxo_apply_delta_reorg.c). Raised where
 * the unwind is declined because the fork point is already final. The
 * predicate is height_is_immutable / reorg_is_allowed
 * (core/modules/validation/include/validation/checkpoint.h) over ZCL_FINALITY_DEPTH
 * = 10 (core/modules/validation/include/validation/main_constants.h). ─────────── */
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(chain.reorg_refused_below_finality,
    "A person must choose; the node deliberately will not. Some peer offered a "
    "chain that branches away from ours BELOW the finality floor - more than 10 "
    "blocks back. Following it would mean un-applying blocks this node already "
    "treats as final, so it refused and is still following its own chain. That "
    "refusal is correct behaviour, not a fault, but it does not resolve on its "
    "own: past 10 blocks the two chains never reconverge, so one of them is "
    "permanently not the one you are on. "
    "FIRST, find out which side you are on: check whether independent peers, "
    "block explorers and the wider network agree with this node's tip. Also "
    "check `dumpstate blocker` for SUSPECTED_NETSPLIT, which fires when this "
    "node already suspects it is on the minority side. "
    "OPTION A - this node is on the chain the network accepts. Do nothing. "
    "Clear the blocker; the deep branch was a stale or hostile peer and "
    "refusing it is exactly what should have happened. Cost: none. "
    "OPTION B - the network moved on without us and this node is the minority. "
    "Re-sync from a height below the fork point, from block bodies, so the "
    "node re-derives the majority chain itself. Cost: a re-fold from that "
    "height, hours of bandwidth. "
    "Never auto-attempted: an automatic escape would have to rewind final "
    "state on the say-so of whichever peer shouted loudest, which is precisely "
    "the attack the finality floor exists to stop. Money that can be un-spent "
    "by a sufficiently patient stranger is not money.")

/* ── First-run wallet refused for want of a terminal
 * (engine/composition/src/boot_wallet_phrase.c, raised from boot_wallet_create_new's
 * REFUSE plan). Nothing has been created at the point this stands: no seed,
 * no keys, no flush. ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(wallet_phrase_no_terminal,
    "A person must choose, because every way forward is a statement about "
    "money only the owner can make. This datadir has no wallet yet, and this "
    "run's stdout is a log file rather than a screen, so the twelve words a "
    "new wallet is born from could only be written into node.log - a file "
    "that is rotated, copied into backups and readable by anyone who can read "
    "the disk. Writing them there would hand over the whole wallet; creating "
    "the wallet without them would leave the owner a balance whose only backup "
    "they were never shown. "
    "OPTION A - run the node once from a terminal. The words are printed one "
    "time, the owner writes them down, and every later start finds the wallet "
    "already there and never asks again. Cost: one interactive start. "
    "OPTION B - declare what this node is for with -operator-lane=dev|soak|"
    "test|copy|standby (or -mint-anchor). A wallet is created with NO recovery "
    "phrase at all - the words are never generated, so they cannot leak - and "
    "the node says so loudly at every start. Cost: this wallet cannot be "
    "recovered from words; it is disposable by declaration. "
    "OPTION C - -wallet-no-phrase-backup, the same bargain as OPTION B for a "
    "lane you do not want to relabel: create it, no phrase, back up node.db "
    "yourself or accept the loss. "
    "Never auto-attempted: picking any of these on the owner's behalf either "
    "prints their spending authority into a log or silently decides that their "
    "money needs no backup.")

/* ── Degraded mode (SUSPECTED_NETSPLIT, raised by
 * engine/services/src/directory_influence_policy.c and driven by
 * engine/conditions/src/netsplit_degraded_mode.c) deliberately has NO row here,
 * and the absence is the honest answer rather than an oversight.
 *
 * blocker_handoff_lookup() only surfaces a decision for an id bound OWNER —
 * "a decision only means anything for a hand-off". SUSPECTED_NETSPLIT has a
 * real automatic remedy: the same condition that raises it folds the verdict
 * in both directions on its poll cadence and clears it the moment the
 * corroborated evidence stops standing. A row here would therefore never
 * reach an operator, and writing decision text that nothing renders is
 * exactly the "looks answered" failure this table was built to avoid.
 *
 * What the operator needs while it stands is carried where they will
 * actually read it — the blocker's own `reason`, which names what is
 * withheld (influence for directory entries finalized at or after the onset
 * height) and, just as importantly, what is NOT (tip-following, relay, the
 * block explorer, wallet viewing). ─────────────────────────────────────── */

/* ── Standing bundle-exporter outage (engine/composition/src/bundle_exporter.c,
 * bx_name_degraded). Qualification and session recovery retry on a bounded
 * backoff; the reason names the current failure. ────────────────────────── */
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(bundle_exporter.degraded,
    "This node is not minting consensus-state bundles. Read the live reason: "
    "it identifies the failure and the newest bundle's age. "
    "The exporter retries qualification and producer-session recovery with "
    "bounded backoff while the node runs; a restart alone cannot supply "
    "missing validation or self-folded coin evidence. "
    "OPTION A - establish the evidence named by the refusal using the "
    "reviewed, copy-first recovery procedure. Export requires proven "
    "authority, a self-folded coin set, and the other source and session "
    "checks. When the stored source epoch matches, a foreign-binary session "
    "may be retired and re-derived by the exporter; a different epoch does "
    "not qualify by assertion. Recovery and minting consume disk and CPU. "
    "OPTION B - keep the current posture and investigate later. The node may "
    "continue its other work under local policy, but no new bundle is minted "
    "while the failure persists. Any usable older bundle grows "
    "staler, increasing the catch-up work for a peer that uses it.")

/* zcode_dht.own_delegation_expired — the ZCODE DHT service disables itself
 * when this node's own delegation.v1 document is past its expiry. Renewal is
 * a signature under the master ZID seed, which this process does not read or
 * hold; the choice below is therefore genuinely a person's, and the DHT
 * service stays off in the meantime rather than serving under an expired
 * claim. ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(zcode_dht.own_delegation_expired,
    "A person must choose; the node cannot renew its own delegation. This "
    "node's ZCODE DHT delegation has expired, so its DHT service is disabled: "
    "it publishes and answers nothing on the DHT. Re-signing requires the "
    "master ZID seed, which this process never reads or holds. "
    "OPTION A - run the zcode.network.delegate command on the machine that "
    "holds the master ZID seed file to issue a fresh delegation, then restart "
    "this node (or wait for its retry) to pick it up. The DHT service comes "
    "back and the blocker clears. Cost: the seed file has to be present, "
    "briefly, wherever that command runs. "
    "OPTION B - leave the delegation expired. Everything else on this node is "
    "unaffected: consensus, relay, wallet and the rest of the commons keep "
    "working. Cost is the DHT surface only — this node stops contributing "
    "records and stops answering lookups, so peers that would have resolved "
    "through it fall back to others. "
    "There is deliberately no option that keeps serving under the expired "
    "document. An expired delegation is exactly the claim other nodes are "
    "supposed to reject, and honouring it locally would only hide that.")
ZCL_BLOCKER_DECISION(sapling_tree.tip_root_missing,
    "The block index has no Sapling root at the boot check endpoint, and the "
    "tip block file could not supply one: boot reads that block's header and "
    "uses its root only when the header hashes to the indexed block. A "
    "validated chain cannot produce this, so the block file or index is "
    "damaged and the loaded Sapling tree cannot be verified. A person must "
    "choose how to restore it. OPTION A - restore the tip block file (for "
    "example by re-fetching it from peers or from a verified snapshot) or "
    "rebuild the block index with a supervised reindex, then restart; a "
    "restart alone does not clear the blocker while the block file stays "
    "unreadable. Cost is a restart and the time to re-fetch or reindex. "
    "OPTION B - leave the node running: consensus, relay and serving are "
    "unaffected, and every shielded spend is still checked against the chain "
    "Sapling root and refused when they disagree, but the wallet refuses "
    "shielded spends while no root is available to check them against. "
    "There is deliberately no automatic repair of the index.")
